# Airsup isolation

`/airsup` is a standalone slice. Keep it easy to delete.

## Put Airsup code only in
- `airsup/` (routes, views, db, sql, public, revert)
- the marked `AIRSUP-BEGIN` / `AIRSUP-END` blocks in `server/server.js`
- `"airsup/**"` in `vercel.json` includeFiles

## Do not
- Import `server/db/supabase.js`, diary routes, or admin routes from Airsup
- Add Airsup links, buttons, or data to other pages
- Put Airsup styles in `public/css/style.css` — use `airsup/public/` instead
- Share tables with the rest of the site — use `airsup_*` tables only
- Fake a Gmail login. Real Google OAuth only (`AIRSUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `AIRSUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`)
- Hardcode Tade (or anyone) as a match. ChatGPT looks at `/airsup/directory` when it needs to find someone new. If the user already named a known person, it does not need to reload the list. Do not require a ChatGPT plugin
- Put complete onboarding answers in the directory. Only approved compact match cards are searchable
- Build embeddings or recommendation graphs. Compare the ~20 compact cards in one model call
- Let an endpoint auto-answer an [A2A-RESPONSE]. REQUESTS are answered. RESPONSES are delivered. RESPONSES are never automatically answered.
- Use Gmail Reply for A2A mail. Always send a new message so the subject stays [A2A-REQUEST] or [A2A-RESPONSE]

## Revert
```bash
node airsup/revert-airsup.js
```
See `airsup/REVERT.md`.
